WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.291
Meet Arctic Linux.

00:00:02.361 --> 00:00:08.046
A calm, keyboard-first desktop built on Fedora, with the Mango tiling window manager.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:11.391
Let's go from the first boot to a day of getting things done.

00:00:12.811 --> 00:00:14.486
Start with a live USB.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:18.428
The boot menu lets you try Arctic Linux or open the installer.

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:22.284
You can explore the desktop before deciding to put it on your computer.

00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:27.235
The live welcome card gives you a few useful shortcuts.

00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:30.942
Keep trying the desktop, or choose Install Arctic Linux.

00:00:31.012 --> 00:00:34.266
The install button is also right there on the top bar.

00:00:35.686 --> 00:00:37.830
The installer starts with your language.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.198
Each screen asks one clear question, and the sidebar shows where you are.

00:00:42.268 --> 00:00:46.625
These installer screens use sample disks, networks, and account details.

00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:51.640
Choose your keyboard layout, then try typing in the test box.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:57.523
Your choice also applies to the live session, so the passwords you enter use the layout you expect.

00:00:58.943 --> 00:01:01.663
Connect to Wi-Fi, or use a network cable.

00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:08.357
Arctic downloads the apps you choose during installation, and carries your Wi-Fi settings into the installed system.

00:01:09.777 --> 00:01:11.578
Next, check your time zone.

00:01:11.648 --> 00:01:16.309
The installer suggests a location, and you can change the region or city.

00:01:16.379 --> 00:01:18.769
Automatic time keeps the clock in sync.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:22.219
Choose your disk and how to install.

00:01:22.289 --> 00:01:24.389
Erasing replaces its contents.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.931
Installing alongside another system is offered when suitable free space is available.

00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:32.281
Back up your files before you continue.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.845
Disk encryption is on by default.

00:01:35.915 --> 00:01:38.699
Create a passphrase, or use the suggested one.

00:01:38.769 --> 00:01:40.956
You'll enter it when the computer starts.

00:01:41.026 --> 00:01:44.599
Keep it safe: forgotten passphrases cannot be recovered.

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:49.763
Create your account, set your sign-in password, and name the computer.

00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:51.784
Automatic login is optional.

00:01:51.854 --> 00:01:55.811
You can also choose to use your account password for the encrypted disk.

00:01:57.231 --> 00:02:01.466
The app picker comes with suggested favourites, but the choices are yours.

00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:05.877
Pick your browser, editor, terminal, file manager, office tools, and more.

00:02:05.947 --> 00:02:08.770
Relevant hardware drivers appear when they're needed.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.575
The summary brings your choices together.

00:02:12.645 --> 00:02:17.007
Check the disk, encryption, account, and apps, and change anything you need.

00:02:17.077 --> 00:02:20.864
Nothing is written to the disk until you confirm the install here.

00:02:22.284 --> 00:02:27.649
The progress screen shows what's happening as Arctic sets up the system and installs your apps.

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:32.530
If an optional app download fails, you can retry it or skip it and add it later.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.800
When setup finishes, review the final notes, restart, and remove the USB.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:44.812
If a driver needs a Secure Boot key, the installer gives you the instructions for that first restart.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.337
Now for everyday life on Arctic.

00:02:48.407 --> 00:02:51.831
The desktop keeps the bar small and the workspace open.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:56.797
Five workspaces help you separate tasks, and the apps you picked are ready to use.

00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:00.569
Press Super and Space to open the launcher.

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:02.548
Type an app name and press Enter.

00:03:02.618 --> 00:03:08.197
It also finds files, open windows, and settings, so you can get to the next task quickly.

00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:11.846
The launcher handles small jobs too.

00:03:11.916 --> 00:03:16.364
Start with an equals sign to calculate, and press Enter to copy the answer.

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:20.605
You can convert units, run commands, or set a reminder for later.

00:03:22.025 --> 00:03:25.662
Open a few windows and Mango arranges them automatically.

00:03:25.732 --> 00:03:28.111
The amber border marks the one you're using.

00:03:28.181 --> 00:03:33.887
Move between windows with Super and the arrow keys, or switch workspaces to separate your tasks.

00:03:35.307 --> 00:03:40.673
Nautilus, also known as GNOME Files, is the graphical file manager in this walkthrough.

00:03:40.743 --> 00:03:44.252
Browse documents and downloads beside your other windows.

00:03:44.322 --> 00:03:47.447
Open your chosen file manager with Super and F.

00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:51.235
Super and Enter opens your terminal.

00:03:51.305 --> 00:03:55.301
The default setup pairs Kitty with Fish and the Arctic fox greeting.

00:03:55.371 --> 00:03:59.861
Flatpak and Nix are preinstalled, alongside Fedora's package tools.

00:04:01.281 --> 00:04:09.697
For everyday apps, Arctic suggests Zen for browsing, Zed for editing, Collabora Office for documents, and VLC for media.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:12.022
These are choices, not requirements.

00:04:12.092 --> 00:04:15.858
You can replace them during installation or later in Settings.

00:04:17.278 --> 00:04:18.611
Need something else?

00:04:18.681 --> 00:04:19.908
Open Get apps.

00:04:19.978 --> 00:04:23.956
Choose Flathub, Fedora packages, a web app, or a terminal tool.

00:04:24.026 --> 00:04:29.520
Installations keep going when you close the launcher, and you get a notification when an app is ready.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.340
Super and S opens Arctic Settings.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.514
Search for a setting instead of hunting through pages.

00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:40.882
Changes apply straight away, and Control and Z undoes the last one.

00:04:42.302 --> 00:04:45.257
Choose the light Winter theme or dark Polar night.

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:53.359
Your own wallpaper can also provide the desktop's colours, carrying them through the shell, window borders, terminal, and supported apps.

00:04:54.779 --> 00:04:58.587
Winter keeps the same layout, with soft snow-coloured surfaces.

00:04:58.657 --> 00:05:03.020
Open the wallpaper picker to choose Arctic artwork or your own pictures.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.492
Built-in wallpapers can follow the theme automatically.

00:05:07.912 --> 00:05:14.558
Quick settings puts the everyday controls together: volume, brightness, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and power mode.

00:05:14.628 --> 00:05:21.166
Night light makes evenings more comfortable, while Keep awake is handy during a presentation or long task.

00:05:22.586 --> 00:05:28.058
The network menu lets you join Wi-Fi and manage saved connections or a VPN.

00:05:28.128 --> 00:05:35.435
Nearby bar menus handle Bluetooth devices, speakers, microphones, and sound levels for individual apps.

00:05:36.855 --> 00:05:41.900
At your desk, arrange monitors and adjust their resolution, scale, and rotation.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.114
Super and P switches screen modes.

00:05:44.184 --> 00:05:49.806
Arctic also handles USB drives, printing, and scanning, with settings when you need them.

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.644
You don't have to memorise every shortcut.

00:05:53.714 --> 00:05:56.455
Super and slash opens a searchable guide.

00:05:56.525 --> 00:06:02.381
Settings lets you add your own shortcuts, choose default apps, and decide what starts when you sign in.

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:08.142
Updates download in the background and install when the computer restarts.

00:06:08.212 --> 00:06:11.850
Settings shows what's waiting and lets you choose the update channel.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:18.074
System snapshots can help restore files after an update, and firmware updates are available when you ask.

00:06:19.494 --> 00:06:22.321
When you step away, Super and L locks the screen.

00:06:22.391 --> 00:06:25.879
The power menu offers suspend, restart, and shut down.

00:06:25.949 --> 00:06:30.397
Arctic also locks before sleeping, with the timing controlled in Settings.

00:06:31.817 --> 00:06:38.228
That's Arctic Linux: a guided installer, a calm desktop, and useful details for everyday work.

00:06:38.298 --> 00:06:42.618
Find the project, downloads, and full documentation on GitHub.

00:06:42.688 --> 00:06:45.194
Try it from a USB, and make it yours.
